+# Clearwater transfer records: unsigned letter, court list and qualified vote record
+
+October 29, 2026. Existing STL01–STL04, SPT01–SPT08, B188/H005 and AUD011/AUD016 remain open. **Two newly acquired official municipal binders supply underlying records missing from the [preceding review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2fa15f1300ded3abc19d06a8efe959b6c01afbed/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-transfer-instructions-2026-10-29/README.md): the unsigned G-0006 transfer letter, a court order with its artifact list, and an explicitly unapproved minute copy reporting authorization.** None establishes completed custody or actual cutting.
+
+## The newly held records
+
+The [December 13 agenda packet](https://edocuments.myclearwater.com/WebLink/edoc/243567/12132010.pdf?dbid=0&repo=Clearwater#page=63), physical pp. 63–77, contains the staff cover memo; a three-page letter dated **November 17, 2010** (pp. 64–66); and an eleven-page court attachment (pp. 67–77). Both letter signature lines are blank. It names **G-0006** and the **January 31, 2007** inventory. The next agenda item starts p. 78. This advances the record from a meeting description to an actual unsigned text; the executed counterpart remains missing. CW-A01 and CW-A04 in [OBSERVATIONS.json](OBSERVATIONS.json).
+
+The court attachment bears **Document 1509 / Filed 07/22/2010**. Its two-page order reserves inspection/testing for September 11 litigation parties or their representatives on ten days notice; the following nine-page Exhibit A lists artifacts. **G-0006 — Steel Tube** appears on printed Exhibit A p. 2 / packet p. 70. This joins the letter's administrative identifier to a court list. It does not authenticate physical origin, delivery, present condition, a public entitlement or a completed test. CW-A05.
+
+The [January 13, 2011 binder](https://edocuments.myclearwater.com/WebLink/edoc/244540/01132011.pdf?dbid=0&repo=Clearwater#page=10) retains a December 16, 2010 minute copy. Packet p. 10 / minute p. 1 is marked **Draft** and **Unapproved**. Item 9.2 on packet p. 19 / minute p. 10 authorizes signing and acceptance; the consent paragraph on packet p. 21 / minute p. 12 reports unanimous approval. Preserve that reported vote together with the draft qualification. It is not an authenticated approved-minute or executed-contract original. CW-B01.
+
+## Conflicting descriptions and incomplete attachments stay unresolved
+
+The staff account in the [earlier work-session minutes](https://clearwater.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?clip_id=1841&view_id=25#page=4) and new agenda p. 63 uses **“holds neither”** while describing indemnification. Letter clause 3, p. 64, instead uses affirmative defense/indemnity/hold-harmless wording; clause 10, p. 65, separately addresses personal liability. All three records remain as found. We do not label the staff text a corrected typo, choose a controlling value, infer misleading intent, or determine legal effect. CW-A02.
+
+Staff describes conditional cutting into two pieces. No express cutting permission was located in the scoped three-page letter; its opening requests the item in its present condition. A separate permission or instruction might exist. Absence from this letter does not establish unauthorized cutting, no permission, actual cutting or concealment. Actual instructions, the signed version and condition/work records are the discriminators. CW-A03.
+
+Clause 6 names **December 4, 2009 or July 22, 2010**, using **“either or both”** and **“both annexed hereto.”** The item attachment acquired here reproduces the July 2010 order. The December 2009 counterpart is still unacquired in this scope. Preserve the wording, dates and assembly question; do not infer that the earlier order never existed or is absent from every unread part of the packet. This is distinct from earlier July 2009, October 2009 and March 2012 order targets. CW-A04.
+
+## Inventory observations and their denominators
+
+The two final Exhibit A pages, packet pp. 76–77 / printed pp. 8–9, supply **104 manually transcribed NIST-labelled entries: 61 + 43**, with 104 distinct supplied labels. [NIST-LABELS.json](NIST-LABELS.json) retains every label and row locator. Descriptions include a washer/nut, aluminum sheathing and multiple columns. A row is not a standard physical-piece or specimen unit. These labels are not yet joined to NIST's native inventory identifiers, the approximately 230 returned items, 236 samples, retained coupons, W14A/B, C12a/b or FEMA Sample 1. Those earlier totals are inherited from the [preservation study](../steel-preservation-decisions-2026-10-27/README.md), not newly validated here. No missing-piece subtraction or fraction is warranted. CW-A07.
+
+On packet p. 71 / printed Exhibit A p. 3, **G-0086 — Steel Plate** appears twice in adjacent rows between G-0083 and G-0087. Both rows remain; we neither deduplicate nor infer two specimens, fabrication or a cause. Packet p. 75 also contains descriptions of symbol cutouts for L-0002 and L-0003. Those labels alone do not date or explain alteration. The full nine-page list was image-read, but only the two NIST pages were completely label-transcribed; no full-list total or completeness census is claimed. CW-A06–A08.
+
+The court's reserved testing condition is concrete contrary evidence to a blanket claim that distribution eliminated every testing right. It does not establish implementation, adequate preservation or successful testing. Original retention/transfer/cutting/condition records and the full inventory/version/alias chain could strengthen or weaken a preservation-failure hypothesis. Neither an innocuous possibility nor an adverse hypothesis resolves the present record conflicts.
+
+## Actual acquisition, reading and testing
+
+The agenda entity is **533 pages / 61,333,079 bytes**, SHA-256 `f2696cfeab6ca20d807923afbe9c0c8ad86e13612b56aa2bc2a64311f8dd1a75`. The later binder is **486 pages / 73,031,332 bytes**, SHA-256 `1b35837e462c6c0e1d585bb3884b32ef81a6d87e9b68c31bb50480085917d549`. **Twenty selected page images were read:** agenda pp. 63–78 and binder pp. 10, 19–21. The other pages were not reviewed in full. Most scanned attachment body text is absent from the PDFs' extractable layer; manual clause/row readings are clearly identified. No OCR, independent reader, native signature/version authentication or physical experiment was performed.
+
+The official [City Clerk page](https://www.myclearwater.com/My-Government/0-City-Departments/City-Clerk) links the public archive. Its search exposed records missed by the general web query. A standalone 21-page minute viewer was located, but its generated export returned a non-PDF entity; the retained binder was a separate observed public route. No cookies were inspected or transferred, no mailbox was accessed, and no authentication bypass was attempted. That access failure and the unavailable native counterpart are not evidence of historical removal. Local receipts preserve the exact successful and failed routes, UTC access times, original bytes and view provenance; raw scans and temporary export URLs are outside the public payload.
+
+`verify_sources_and_rows.py` checks the three held entity hashes/page counts, exposed attachment/header markers and the accounting of supplied manual labels/duplicate rows. Its output [RESULTS.json](RESULTS.json) is a documentary/structural check, not independent validation of image readings or historical events. A failed image-grid diagnostic was not used to corroborate the manual count. [SOURCES.json](SOURCES.json), [OBSERVATIONS.json](OBSERVATIONS.json) and the checklist identify exact source roles and scope. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) is the additive note diff; predecessors and raw sources are unchanged.
+
+[OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) advances the now-held unsigned letter, court attachment/list and draft vote account without silently closing the missing approved/executed/custody records. Full 2004/2006/2007 inventory editions and their conflicting dates remain unresolved. FAA correction/receipt/signed disposition, telephone native joins, and the technical owners' recorder/materials tests remain open; all eighteen original requirements and five-track acceptance criteria are preserved.
+
+Only reviewed original research, safe source pins, manual nonpersonal labels, code/results and diffs enter this public addition. Raw sources, signatures/contact data, unrelated records, private correspondence, internal coordination and strategy remain local. No outreach, fees, new request/filing, physical testing, deletion, private push, merge or history rewrite occurred. Acquisition, documentary checks and publication are separate partial milestones; the substantive goal remains open.
